+Human-client revision evidence, October 7, 2026
+
+This is a guided revision of reviewed Chapter 2 cc1bec45, not another cold
+whole-chapter attempt. Sources and authored helpers are in source-read-ledger.json.
+The student did not read first-edition implementations or grader internals.
+
+Three paid actual-terminal sessions: anthropic-main, openai-main, gemini-main.
+Each launch.json records command, date, selected model, exact Go source hashes,
+binary hash, mode and exit. terminal.txt is the actual macOS script transcript
+inside a persistent tool PTY. The coder observed each model reply before typing
+the next model prompt; this was not Bill's participation. The launch helper
+supplies no conversational input. Discovery receipts list freshly returned IDs.
+
+Actions and observable outcomes on all three providers:
+- Ordinary text asks for an invented code name; readable answer and next prompt.
+- /ephemeral records one-request marker and acknowledges without HTTP.
+- Follow-up recalls the exact earlier name and reverses it on a second line;
+  actual newlines are displayed. All three answers passed exact comparison.
+- /usage displays four named counts; /history shows seven numbered event kinds
+  and explicitly states no tool_returned target exists in this no-tool chapter.
+- /help displays every command, slash escape, UTF-8 byte limit, LF/CRLF treatment.
+- Blank input, empty /ephemeral, malformed /redact and unknown command all return
+  prompts; no extra log event or model request. Later submission still works.
+- //help is sent as literal /help text and each real model replies SLASH-OK.
+- /quit reports final disjoint usage and exits zero after exactly three requests.
+- Separate provider-configured actual-terminal sessions exercise Ctrl-D EOF with
+  zero totals and no paid request. Default TTY selection is demonstrated with
+  Anthropic main, OpenAI EOF and Gemini EOF; explicit chat is shown for each.
+
+receipts.json contains per-response requested/returned identities and totals.
+verify-receipts.py verifies those receipts and reconstructs requests offline from
+actual log prefixes: ephemeral marker absent/present/absent, consumed []/[4]/[].
+These reconstructed requests are not claimed to be intercepted HTTP bodies.
+It also proves offline dump equality and byte-identical repeated final rendering.
+Actual key values were scanned against all saved evidence: no matches.
+
+Local controls, separate from paid success:
+- *-invalid-target are actual terminal sessions selecting each provider but
+  making no HTTP request. /redact 1 1 ... fails nonzero without final usage.
+  Initial inherited diagnostic is safely vague: 'invalid event or conversation
+  transition'. Flagged to independent review for a useful static reason.
+- cmd/chat_test.go protects exact 1 MiB LF/CRLF/EOF input, over-limit and invalid
+  UTF-8 refusal; local syntax/no-event behavior; multiline/plain output; empty
+  and tool-only notices; four counts; EOF/quit; pre-banner configuration failure;
+  safe non-200 failure; unchanged exact explicit/default protocol bytes and
+  byte-identical HTTP bodies for equivalent human/machine requests.
+- Its controlled-result test feeds public Append facts, uses /history to find
+  call-visible at sequence 3, redacts that target through human commands, and
+  confirms context rendering removes content. This is no real tool execution.
+- Previous machine/public-consumer paid receipts retain their original meaning;
+  no unrelated paid tool, provider-switch or GUI behavior was rerun or invented.
+  The optional GUI remains a fake-tested stub with no browser transport.
+
+initial-checks.json and initial-grade.txt record successful checks in all three
